  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe status strip formatted the operation count as `\"{ops_n} Operations\"`. With one operation it read \"1 Operations\".\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs`: the label uses the existing browser helper `browser_tree::count(ops_n, \"Operation\")`. It reads \"1 Operation\" for one operation and \"N Operations\" for more. The label still shows only when `ops_n > 0`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/browser_tree.rs`: `count` is now `pub(super)`, with a doc line. Its behaviour does not change, thus the browser suffixes (\"1 tool\", \"2 operations\") stay the same.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural/ops_count.rs`: a new structural test. `panes.rs` and `structural.rs` are already longer than 400 lines. The change adds no line to `panes.rs`, and the test is a new submodule in the same form as `structural/donate.rs`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinned by `the_status_strip_counts_one_operation_in_the_singular_and_two_in_the_plural` (`camcraft-ui` lib, `egui_app::tests::structural::ops_count`):\n- The seed document has one operation. The strip paints \"1 Operation\".\n- The test adds a second operation (`Contour2`, through `CommandKind::CreateOperation`). The strip paints \"2 Operations\".\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base main`, Linux, 12 cores):\n- `ui build (--no-run)`: ok.\n- `ui suites: boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `sinker_setup`, `tap_hand`, `theme_example`, `theme_files`, `waterjet_tool`: ok.\n- `ui suites: lib`: 1169 passed, 1 failed. The new test passed. The failed test is `diag::tests::diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level` (`crates/ui/src/diag.rs`, not touched by this PR). Its INFO line was missing from the captured output, while the WARN line was there.\n- That test passed 3 of 3 times alone. Two more full `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` runs gave 1170 passed, 0 failed. Thus it is flaky in a parallel run, and this PR does not cause it.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nThe gate ran on the same `crates/` tree on top of PROCESS_VERSION 101. The PR branch is that commit on `v0.24.0`, without the process sync commit of the fork. `git merge-tree` with `upstream/main` shows no conflict.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No visual check of the strip in the running app. The test reads the painted text of the frame.\n- No snapshot PNG changes (release lane).\n\n## Process notes\n\n- Fork synced at v0.24.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 101).\n- No context scout ran. This session did its own searches (the `work-issue` fallback).\n\nChangelog: Status strip: one operation reads \"1 Operation\", not \"1 Operations\".\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #2340\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
